# Pairs with RLinearizedTerminals. The receiver's post-gate fan-out applies a
# commit terminal to each leaf whatever its registry recorded. For an aborted
# saga a receiver leaf then holds a commit terminal the origin never decided.
# The buckets are still discarded (the projection is untouched on the abort
# path), so no read changes; only the terminal the leaf remembers is wrong,
# which is what makes this property's and RStrictIsolation's pairings distinct.
MODULE: RLinearizedTerminalsFanOutAppliesCommit
TARGET: RLinearizedTerminals
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the receiver fan-out applies a commit terminal regardless of the recorded outcome
PERTURBS: ReceiverFanOut

--- FIND
       ELSE /\ rterm' = [rterm EXCEPT ![k] = Kind(rdec[TreeOf(k)])]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the leaf is always told "commit".
       ELSE /\ rterm' = [rterm EXCEPT ![k] = "commit"]
--- END
